review:83488_r4 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "The Pantheon In Paris France The Pantheon comes from the Greek word Pantheon, meaning \"All the Gods\" and is a building in the Latin Quarter in Paris, France." ;
    schema:about place:83488 .

review:83488_r5 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "This is Paris’s oldest theatre. Its facade features an art deco rendering of a vintage projector. New and often obscure international films are screened here. Click here for more." ;
    schema:about place:83488 .

review:83488_r6 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Ce monument néo-classique a vocation à honorer des personnages ayant marqué l'Histoire de France. On y trouve aussi un pendule de Foucault, commémorant l'expérience de 1851." ;
    schema:about place:83488 .

review:83488_r7 a schema:Review ;
    schema:author "Anonymous" ;
    schema:reviewBody "Try to get the tour. It's only in french, but it's good. This monument is not so visited, but beautiful and has a lot of french history and its main \"actors\"" ;
    schema:about place:83488 .

review:83488_r8 a schema:Review ;
